    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Title: Program to Implement Selection Sort and Bubble Sort."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Problem Statement:"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Write a program to store the first-year percentage of students in an array. Write function for sorting array of floating-point numbers in ascending order using-Selection Sort Bubble sort and display top five scores."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Outcomes"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Students will be able to write programs for sorting data in arrays."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Understand the working and efficiency of selection and bubble sort algorithms."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Software & Hardware Requirements"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Theory :"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Selection Sort"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "The selection sort algorithm sorts an array by repeatedly finding the minimum element (considering ascending order) from unsorted part and putting it at the beginning. The algorithm maintains two subarrays in a given array. The subarray which is already sorted. Remaining subarray which is unsorted. In every iteration of selection sort, the minimum element (considering ascending order) from the unsorted subarray is picked and moved to the sorted subarray."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Selection Sort Algorithm"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "Algorithm selectionSort ( low, high )"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "{ //a[low : high] is an array of size n i=0, j=0, temp=0, ; for i: =low to high do"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "{"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "minindex = i;"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "for j: =i+1 to high do"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "{"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "if( a[j] < a[minindex] ) then minindex := j;"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "temp := a[i];"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "a[i] := a[minindex]; a[minindex] := temp;"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "Example: The selection sort algorithm sorts an array by repeatedly finding the minimum element (considering ascending order) from unsorted part and putting it at the beginning. In every iteration of selection sort, the minimum element from the unsorted sub-array is picked and moved to the sorted sub- array."
    },
