    {
      "style": "Heading 2",
      "text": "Bubble Sort"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "Bubble sort is a simple sorting algorithm. This sorting algorithm is comparison- based algorithm in which each pair of adjacent elements is compared and the elements are swapped if they are not in order. This algorithm is not suitable for large data sets as its average and worst case complexity is of Ο(n2) where n is the number of items."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 2",
      "text": "Bubble Sort Algorithm"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "Algorithm bubblesort ( x[], n)"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "{ // x[1:n] is an array of n elementsfor i := 0 to n do"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": " {"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "for j := 0 to n–i-1 d0"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "{"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "if (x[j] > x[j+1])"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "{"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "text": "temp = x[j]; x[j] = x[j+1]; x[j+1] = temp;"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "}"
